WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.856
Warm outreach is value plus a clear ask.

00:00:02.856 --> 00:00:04.999
Weird outreach is guilt and fog.

00:00:04.999 --> 00:00:08.212
This lesson is about warm outreach that isn't weird.

00:00:08.212 --> 00:00:09.640
Value + clear ask.

00:00:09.640 --> 00:00:12.139
Do not treat this as theory only.

00:00:12.139 --> 00:00:15.710
Treat it as a move you can run this week.

00:00:15.710 --> 00:00:21.065
By the end, you should be able to act without waiting for a perfect plan.

00:00:21.065 --> 00:00:24.993
Keep the DigProg habit: watch, practice, then take one real action.

00:00:24.993 --> 00:00:28.920
Stay practical: send five messages before you optimize branding or tools.

00:00:29.240 --> 00:00:34.280
Lead with why you are writing, one useful note, and one simple next step.

00:00:34.280 --> 00:00:36.440
Remember the objective: send five messages.

00:00:36.440 --> 00:00:40.400
Write the idea in your own words before you move on.

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:44.720
Name one concrete next action you can finish in under an hour.

00:00:44.720 --> 00:00:48.680
Avoid vanity work that feels busy but does not create proof.

00:00:48.680 --> 00:00:53.000
If something is unclear, simplify the promise and try a smaller version.

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:55.520
Talk to a real person when possible.

00:00:55.520 --> 00:00:56.960
Feedback beats guessing alone.

00:00:57.280 --> 00:01:00.349
Send five messages this week to reachable people.

00:01:00.349 --> 00:01:02.268
Real sends beat perfect drafts.

